hey guys it's Jenna here I love snacks  and I do enjoy checking thumb up if you  do well munches we got to make sure that  our snacks are healthy without packing  on high amount of extra calories which  may leave you feeling bloated or  regretful in the morning so be sure to  watch this video through add it to your  favourite playlist because I'm going to  share with you three ingredient vegan  healthy snack bites really really easy  no baking or cooking is required and you  can make them in less than five minutes  trust me you would want to eat the  entire batch after taking your first  bite so we want if you need a quick and  easy to consume pre or post-workout  snack with protein and carbs then you  got to make these mini protein cupcakes  the three wholesome ingredients which  will nourish your body for a good  workout are one cup of rolled oats two  scoops of protein powder and one large  banana sliced add oats and protein  powder into a food processor process  very quickly just until the oats are  slightly chopped but not completely  smooth then add the banana and continue  to process until well combined transfer  the mixture evenly into 12 mini cupcake  liners store them in a container and  freeze them up before consuming allow  them to defrost for about five minutes  if you want to bring them out with you  then choose to pick them in the oven for  about 10 to 15 minutes a serving of  three mini cupcakes contain 167 calories  15 gram of protein and 23 gram of carbs  a really great pre or post-workout snack  you can even Jessop this basic recipe  and mix in some dried fruits chopped  nuts or seeds I'm sure most of you have  come across the three ingredient energy  bar I'm going to also share this with  you because it is so versatile and you  can keep making it with different  ingredients this recipe calls for three  basic ingredients 1 cup of dates prunes  or figs because they are sticky the  other main ingredient to hold the  mixture together  I used prunes one cup of  fruits of your choice this will give you  the chewy texture and natural sweetness  I used goji berries and one cup of nuts  or seeds of your choice this is to add  crunchiness into the bar I opted for  sunflower seeds in a food processor add  in the prunes and process until they  begin to form a paste then mix in the  goji berries and sunflower seeds  continue to process very quickly just to  combine the ingredients the mixture may  loosen up with the addition of fruits  and nuts and the texture will be chunky  but that's okay transfer the mixture  onto a parchment-lined pan and press  down firmly to form a thick square  because my pan is rather large I will  only use half of it use a clean wrap  because the mixture is very sticky wrap  and chill in the fridge for about 1 to 2  hours or until firm once firm cuts into  12 even bars store these energy bars in  the fridge until ready for consumption  it will last up to two weeks prunes  contain less sugar than dates so they  are a good option if you are looking to  keep the sugar content low I like to  carry one energy bar in my back in case  if I need a quick energy boost to keep  me going I have a healthy option to turn  to bear in mind that they are sticky but  so yummy so try this recipe and keep  experimenting with different  combinations let me know your favorite  combination in the comments below  I love soft baked cookies so I have to  look for a healthier option this mini  cookie dough balls are soft naturally  sweetened and made only with real food  the three main ingredients are one can  of chickpeas washed and drain  cut a cup of peanut butter and 2  tablespoons of maple syrup or honey  in a food processor mix in the chickpeas  peanut butter and maple syrup process on  high speed and to smooth and well  combined if you do not have a powerful  blender like me then you may need to  scrape off the side and just keep  blending you should have a rather smooth  dough but don't worry if it's a little  bit chunky  measure about one tablespoon of dough  roll and form into mini balls  this should make about 16 mini cookie  dough balls place them on baking sheet  or cupcake liners you may choose to  freeze them until solid or chill in the  fridge for a softer texture or just eat  immediately they are so good  chickpeas are used as the foundation to  this healthy cookie dough but don't  worry you can barely taste the chickpeas  peanut butter adds a slight nutty flavor  which can also be replaced with any nut  or seed butter of your choice each  cookie dough bites is only 49 calories  and if you want to you can even bake  them for a crunchy texture all these  recipes are super easy and versatile  with the three basic ingredients you can  jazz it up with all kinds of add-ins to  suit your tastes such as chocolate chips  chia seeds shredded coconut any nuts or  seeds and more I would also like to give  a shout out to the National Academy of  Sports Medicine &amp; ASM for providing me  with a solid foundation to learn more  about Fitness food healthy living and to  share my knowledge and passion with you  guys so if you're interested in healthy  living or to help others to get healthy  the NASM is currently offering a 14-day  free trial to the online personal  training costs I have to share this  opportunity with you guys because I  think is a really good platform to  kick-start your fitness journey or  career so if you're interested linked  and more information is in my  description box and be sure to try all  these recipes let me know which is a  favorite in the comments below share and  like this video as well all the best  you
 

